Short:        IPP/AirPrint printing driver and setup tool
Author:       Darren Banfi (boingball)
Uploader:     boingball gmail com (Darren Banfi)
Type:         util/misc
Version:      1.0.0
Requires:     68000+; TCP/IP stack (bsdsocket.library) for all printing;
              AmigaOS 3.5+, or 3.2 with an updated printer.device, for the
              DEVS:Printers/MintPRINT driver's V44 extended driver tags
Architecture: m68k-amigaos >= 3.5.0

MintPRINT
=========

MintPRINT lets classic AmigaOS applications print to modern network
printers - the same IPP/AirPrint printers phones and modern computers
already use - with no printer-specific software needed on the printer
side. It is a real DEVS:Printers/ printer.device driver plus MintPrint
Settings, a GUI setup and test tool.

Print from any application that already supports Amiga's standard printer
graphics dump (MultiView, GraphicDump, and most paint/DTP software) - the
driver converts printer.device's raster callbacks into a JPEG, PWG Raster,
or PDF document and submits it straight to the printer's IPP endpoint over
the network.

This archive contains one drawer:

  MintPRINT/
    MintPrintSettings       GUI setup, discovery and test tool
    MintPRINT                the printer.device driver

Features
--------

  - Real DEVS:Printers/ driver - no add-on print spooler required
  - Prints JPEG, PWG Raster, or PDF, selectable per printer
  - LAN printer discovery (SSDP and mDNS)
  - IPP capability query - reads the printer's supported media, trays,
    colour modes, quality settings, and document formats directly
  - Up to eight saved printer profiles (Unit0-Unit7), with one made
    active for printing at a time
  - Printer make/model shown after a successful query
  - Built-in test page, printed straight through printer.device
  - Warns if a printer advertises none of the formats MintPRINT can
    produce, with a pointer to reporting it for support
  - Detects and offers to install or update the driver automatically

Requirements
------------

  - AmigaOS 3.0 or later for MintPrint Settings itself (gadtools.library,
    intuition.library, graphics.library v39)
  - AmigaOS 3.5 or later - or 3.2 with an updated printer.device - for
    the driver's V44 extended driver tags to take effect
  - A running TCP/IP stack providing bsdsocket.library - required for
    every printing path, since MintPRINT always talks to the printer over
    the network
  - A network-attached printer supporting IPP, with AirPrint or "IPP
    Everywhere" support covering the vast majority of network printers
    from roughly the last decade

Installation
------------

Extract the archive. Copy the MintPRINT drawer wherever you like, then run
MintPrintSettings. On first run it detects that DEVS:Printers/MintPRINT is
missing and offers to install it; on later runs, if a newer driver is
bundled next to MintPrintSettings than the one installed, it offers to
update it instead.

**Reboot after any driver install or update** - a driver segment already
resident in memory will not pick up a replaced file until then. This is a
real AmigaOS printer.device driver, and the OS does not reload the file
just because it changed.

After rebooting, open Prefs/Printer, select MintPRINT as your printer,
and configure your printer's IP/host, IPP path, and document format in
MintPrint Settings. Query Printer (or Discover, to search the LAN) reads
back the printer's real capabilities and fills the rest in.

Reporting a problem
--------------------

If MintPrint Settings' Query reports that your printer doesn't support
any format MintPRINT can produce, or printing otherwise fails, please
open an issue at:

  https://github.com/boingball/MintPRINT/issues

and attach the output of windows_ipp_probe.py (included in the source
repository) run against your printer from a Windows PC on the same
network - it isolates printer-side from Amiga-side issues without needing
any Amiga-specific tooling.

